470
00:34:23.111 --> 00:34:24.000
<v TOWNER>[Disagrees]

471
00:34:24.000 --> 00:34:27.341
<v AMBROSE>They said it was in a store.

472
00:34:27.341 --> 00:34:30.682
<v TOWNER>Must have been uncle Ira's, Ira Garett.

473
00:34:30.682 --> 00:34:34.977
<v ARSENEAULT>Someone told me Jim Moss had the post office.

474
00:34:34.977 --> 00:34:37.364
<v AMBROSE>Okay, then that's Pete's daddy.

475
00:34:37.364 --> 00:34:39.273
That's Pete Moss' daddy.

476
00:34:39.273 --> 00:34:45.000
<v TOWNER>I didn't think any of them people knew how to read.

477
00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:52.703
<v AMBROSE>Well how did grandpa, and grandma, and all them learn how to read and write?

478
00:34:52.703 --> 00:34:54.757
<v TOWNER>I have no idea.

479
00:34:54.757 --> 00:34:58.351
<v AMBROSE>Grandma Perkins read and wrote letters [ . . . ?] [write?].

480
00:34:58.351 --> 00:34:59.892
<v TOWNER>Yes, I know.

481
00:34:59.892 --> 00:35:04.000
<v AMBROSE>I assume granny could read and write.

482
00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:05.330
<v TOWNER>I don't know.

483
00:35:05.330 --> 00:35:10.205
<v AMBROSE>Grandma Towner read and write . . . I mean could read and write.

484
00:35:10.205 --> 00:35:14.636
Now I know how she learned to read and write.

485
00:35:14.636 --> 00:35:18.182
She went to school with her daddy's children.

486
00:35:18.182 --> 00:35:23.057
When the teachers came and would teach them, they taught her.

487
00:35:23.057 --> 00:35:24.830
That's how she learned.

488
00:35:24.830 --> 00:35:30.591
But Grandma Perkins . . . and I don't know how they learned, but they all . . .

489
00:35:30.591 --> 00:35:32.807
<v TOWNER>Learned to read and write.

490
00:35:32.807 --> 00:35:34.136
<v AMBROSE>They were literate.

491
00:35:34.136 --> 00:35:37.239
So maybe James Perkins could . . . James Moss.

492
00:35:37.239 --> 00:35:39.455
That's who gave the land.

493
00:35:39.455 --> 00:35:42.114
Well that's Jim Moss, Pete's daddy.

494
00:35:42.114 --> 00:35:43.000
<v TOWNER>Yes.

495
00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:46.429
<v AMBROSE>So maybe he could read and write, too.

496
00:35:46.429 --> 00:35:47.714
I don't know.

497
00:35:47.714 --> 00:35:48.571
<v TOWNER>Maybe so.

498
00:35:48.571 --> 00:35:55.000
<v AMBROSE>I need to get a copy of that to see if he signed his name,

499
00:35:55.000 --> 00:36:01.429
