500
00:36:01.429 --> 00:36:02.714
<v TOWNER>To the deed?

501
00:36:02.714 --> 00:36:03.143
<v AMBROSE>Yes.

502
00:36:03.143 --> 00:36:04.429
Uncle [Irvin?] wrote.

503
00:36:04.429 --> 00:36:05.714
He could write.

504
00:36:05.714 --> 00:36:07.000
All of them.

505
00:36:07.000 --> 00:36:10.000
Grandpa . . . [?] was secretary of the church.

506
00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:10.568
<v TOWNER>Oh really?

507
00:36:10.568 --> 00:36:16.812
<v AMBROSE>[Agrees] And I hate it so much because when uncle [Irvin?] died and they went over there and cleaned out his stuff,

508
00:36:16.812 --> 00:36:24.192
Bobby was over there with him and she said she remembered they had these ledgers and they had all kind of rules and regulations in there.

509
00:36:24.192 --> 00:36:30.721
She said she was a little girl but she remembered reading on how far you had to be from the church to spit,

510
00:36:30.721 --> 00:36:32.991
because people would chew tobacco during that time.

511
00:36:32.991 --> 00:36:35.546
How far you had to be from the church.

512
00:36:35.546 --> 00:36:37.817
<c.p>UNIDENTIFIED MALE 1: That’s like they're smoking now.

513
00:36:37.817 --> 00:36:41.507
<v AMBROSE>Yes, how far you had to be away from the church to smoke.

514
00:36:41.507 --> 00:36:44.061
All those rules and regulations was in that book.

515
00:36:44.061 --> 00:36:50.022
But they ended up burning them because Daddy didn't realize the value . . . how valuable they were or they could have been.

516
00:36:50.022 --> 00:36:55.131
So they would just clean out uncle [Irvin's?] things and they tossed them when [Irvin?] was a secretary.

517
00:36:55.131 --> 00:37:01.943
So a lot of that stuff he wrote or people prior to him, the church secretary prior to him, they wrote all these rules.

518
00:37:01.943 --> 00:37:04.214
So the church always had rules and regulations.

519
00:37:04.214 --> 00:37:08.755
And when I say how far away you had to be from the church to spit,

520
00:37:08.755 --> 00:37:13.865
then after thinking about it I said, "Well that's true," because a lot of them did chew tobacco.

521
00:37:13.865 --> 00:37:16.500
<c.p>UNIDENTIFIED MALE 1: You writing down what she said?

522
00:37:16.500 --> 00:37:17.000
<v DIGILORMO>Oh, no.

523
00:37:17.000 --> 00:37:19.000
<v AMBROSE>And they couldn't spit right around the church.

524
00:37:19.000 --> 00:37:20.750
<v DIGILORMO>[ . . . ?] I'm just taking a couple of notes.

525
00:37:20.750 --> 00:37:21.750
<c.p>UNIDENTIFIED MALE 1: Okay.

526
00:37:21.750 --> 00:37:23.000
I was just wondering.

527
00:37:23.000 --> 00:37:24.070
<v TOWNER>That makes sense.

528
00:37:24.070 --> 00:37:24.426
<v AMBROSE>Yes.

529
00:37:24.426 --> 00:37:26.209
So I said, "Oh boy,

530
00:37:26.209 --> 00:37:32.270
[ . . . ?] sorry being through all that stuff away that would have been invaluable what we could have found."

531
00:37:32.270 --> 00:37:35.835
So that's why I wanted to go through the church.

532
00:37:35.835 --> 00:37:39.400
Some of the records they have still at the church.

533
00:37:39.400 --> 00:37:46.174
But they're so dusty when I go in that room it makes my nose runny, makes me feel bad.

534
00:37:46.174 --> 00:37:56.513
But I'm going to try to go in there so that I can . . . I can see what else I can find before they get through with all their history.

535
00:37:56.513 --> 00:37:57.226
<v TOWNER>Oh, okay.

536
00:37:57.226 --> 00:38:04.000
<v AMBROSE>But did you tell her where your grandparents came from right along the side of the railroad tracks?

537
00:38:04.000 --> 00:38:04.434
<v TOWNER>[Agrees]

538
00:38:04.434 --> 00:38:07.038
<v AMBROSE>What was it called down there?

539
00:38:07.038 --> 00:38:08.774
<v TOWNER>Well it . . . Bayou d'Inde.

540
00:38:08.774 --> 00:38:10.509
<v AMBROSE>That was Bayou d'Inde.

541
00:38:10.509 --> 00:38:17.887
So, okay, where was it where those others . . . those . . . on Highway 90, that was called something too.

542
00:38:17.887 --> 00:38:20.057
That was called Bayou d'Inde.

543
00:38:20.057 --> 00:38:26.132
But where those Hayes were, Ms. Hayes and them, was that called something too?

544
00:38:26.132 --> 00:38:27.000
<v TOWNER>[Disagrees]

545
00:38:27.000 --> 00:38:29.333
<v AMBROSE>Across the road from where your grandmother . . .

546
00:38:29.333 --> 00:38:30.333
<v TOWNER>It was always . . .

547
00:38:30.333 --> 00:38:31.000
<v AMBROSE>Bayou d'Inde.

548
00:38:31.000 --> 00:38:33.000
<v TOWNER>Well they didn't say Bayou d'Inde.

549
00:38:33.000 --> 00:38:35.333
They just said Bayou [Pronounced “Buy”] d'Inde.

550
00:38:35.333 --> 00:38:38.000
<v AMBROSE>I never knew it was Bayou d'Inde.

551
00:38:38.000 --> 00:38:39.444
<v TOWNER>I didn't either.

552
00:38:39.444 --> 00:38:41.852
<v AMBROSE>I was grown and married.

553
00:38:41.852 --> 00:38:44.741
All they said was "Buy d'Inde".

554
00:38:44.741 --> 00:38:48.111
<v TOWNER>[Agrees] It's all the same really. [laughs]

555
00:38:48.111 --> 00:38:48.593
<v AMBROSE>Yes.

556
00:38:48.593 --> 00:38:51.000
But it's Bayou d'Inde.

557
00:38:51.000 --> 00:38:55.525
<v TOWNER>[Agrees] Now you wouldn't even know it was any homes down there.

558
00:38:55.525 --> 00:38:56.279
<v AMBROSE>No markers.

559
00:38:56.279 --> 00:39:02.311
I’m just so sorry we didn’t go and take pictures of all the places and names.

560
00:39:02.311 --> 00:39:05.328
I’m just so sorry I didn’t do that.

561
00:39:05.328 --> 00:39:10.230
I tried to get Butch to go with me, but then he decided

562
00:39:10.230 --> 00:39:13.246
<c.p>he would take somebody from the TV station.

563
00:39:13.246 --> 00:39:18.525
When they came out there to interview them . . . what is his name from KPLC?

564
00:39:18.525 --> 00:39:19.656
He took him.

565
00:39:19.656 --> 00:39:27.197
But I wanted to go to each place and take a picture of where the house was in the family,

566
00:39:27.197 --> 00:39:37.000
because I started a sort of like map down Highway . . . down the Old Spanish Trail where each person stayed in reference to what’s there now.

567
00:39:37.000 --> 00:39:37.387
<v TOWNER>Oh, okay.

568
00:39:37.387 --> 00:39:38.935
<v AMBROSE>But then [Carl?] would have to help me.

569
00:39:38.935 --> 00:39:39.903
<v TOWNER>That would have been nice.

570
00:39:39.903 --> 00:39:42.419
<v AMBROSE>Yes, because he came . . . [Carl?] kind of helped me with some of them.

571
00:39:42.419 --> 00:39:43.000
<v TOWNER>Oh really?

572
00:39:43.000 --> 00:39:46.978
<v AMBROSE>Well, because I couldn't remember where Low Top Inn was.

573
00:39:46.978 --> 00:39:54.538
I knew it was past Conoco, but before you got to Trousdale Road, but I couldn't remember exactly where.

574
00:39:54.538 --> 00:39:59.312
So then he told me it was the . . . the church, the Sullivans.

575
00:39:59.312 --> 00:40:01.699
And I remember uncle Irvin's wife [ . . . ?]

